--- !u!114 &376775044
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1998800283}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7bfe88a1dd63542739086a9c9935c46a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Lalim.Mechanics.StatueDialogueRouter
  _deityName: Amansinaya
  _questLines:
  - speakerName: Amansinaya
    text: Hush, little diver. Long ago the fisherfolk whistled to me before they
      cast their nets, and I answered them with silver shoals.
    isPlayer: 0
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Amansinaya
    text: "\"Kasump\xE2 ak\xF3,\" they would say. \"I am your sworn friend.\" And
      they never ate the first catch. They gave it back, so the sea would give again."
    isPlayer: 0
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: '{player}'
    text: "The water stings\u2026 and everything here is so grey."
    isPlayer: 1
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Amansinaya
    text: Now the land sends down what it no longer wants. Plastic, glass, metal.
      My shallows choke on it, and the water has turned to poison.
    isPlayer: 0
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Amansinaya
    text: Gather every piece you find. Leave nothing behind, not one shard.
    isPlayer: 0
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Amansinaya
    text: If your eyes fail you, awaken the spirit sight. What is hidden will glow,
      and a light will lead you to it.
    isPlayer: 0
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Amansinaya
    text: Then lay each piece in its rightful bowl. What is sorted truly can be made
      new again. Go, and be quick. The poison does not wait.
    isPlayer: 0
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  _closingLines:
  - speakerName: Amansinaya
    text: 'Take this as well. It reads the water''s hidden moods: its sourness, its
      salt, its warmth.'
    isPlayer: 0
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Amansinaya
    text: Haik, who once guided sailors through every storm, waits beyond the next
      gate. His waters are sick in ways the eye cannot see.
    isPlayer: 0
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: '{player}'
    text: I'll find him.
    isPlayer: 1
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Amansinaya
    text: Remember the fisherfolk's way, {player}. Take only what you need, and give
      back the first of what you are given.
    isPlayer: 0
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  _idleLines:
  - speakerName: Amansinaya
    text: The fisherfolk will whistle for me again one day. Go on, Haik is waiting.
    isPlayer: 0
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  _barks:
  - key: altar_rises
    lines:
    - speakerName: Amansinaya
      text: 'Every wound lifted. Now: plastic, glass, metal. Choose with care. The
        sea remembers.'
      isPlayer: 0
      portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - key: relic_gift
    lines:
    - speakerName: Amansinaya
      text: Do you feel it? My shallows taste sweet again.
      isPlayer: 0
      portrait: {fileID: 0}
    - speakerName: Amansinaya
      text: Every shard lifted, every piece laid in its rightful bowl. You have a
        fisherfolk's heart, {player}.
      isPlayer: 0
      portrait: {fileID: 0}
    - speakerName: Amansinaya
      text: Take this, the Radiant Conch. The fisherfolk blew it across the water
        to call one another home.
      isPlayer: 0
      portrait: {fileID: 0}
    - speakerName: '{player}'
      text: "It's glowing\u2026 like there's light inside it."
      isPlayer: 1
      portrait: {fileID: 0}
    - speakerName: Amansinaya
      text: Keep it close. One day, waters far from here will need its call.
      isPlayer: 0
      portrait: {fileID: 0}
  _talkPoint: {fileID: 1936409811}
  _dugongPoint: {fileID: 575387180}
  _talkCamera: {fileID: 1517495439}
  _frameWithin: 30
  _fadeSeconds: 0.35
  onIntroComplete:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
