--- !u!114 &878696728
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 859860216}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7bfe88a1dd63542739086a9c9935c46a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Lalim.Mechanics.StatueDialogueRouter
  _deityName: Haik
  _questLines:
  - speakerName: Haik
    text: "A traveller\u2026 Few find their way to me now. Sailors once called my
      name before every voyage, and I calmed the storms in their path."
    isPlayer: 0
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Haik
    text: But no storm has frightened me like this one. It has no wind, no thunder.
      It hides inside the water itself.
    isPlayer: 0
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: '{player}'
    text: Amansinaya gave me this kit. She said your waters are sick in ways I can't
      see.
    isPlayer: 1
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Haik
    text: Then read them the way a navigator reads the sky. Three places in my waters
      speak loudest. Test each one.
    isPlayer: 0
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Haik
    text: 'Healthy reef water is only a little bitter: a pH between 7.9 and 8.4.
      Its salt sits between 33 and 37 parts per thousand.'
    isPlayer: 0
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Haik
    text: 'It is warm, but never hot: 24 to 29 degrees. Any warmer and the coral
      sickens and turns white.'
    isPlayer: 0
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Haik
    text: Stop each needle when it sits in the green. Only a true reading can guide
      a true course.
    isPlayer: 0
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  _closingLines:
  - speakerName: Haik
    text: Go deeper, traveller. Neguno rules the waters past the last gate. He is
      not as gentle as I am.
    isPlayer: 0
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  _idleLines:
  - speakerName: Haik
    text: Steady hands, true readings. Neguno is waiting below.
    isPlayer: 0
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
  _barks:
  - key: readings_done
    lines:
    - speakerName: Haik
      text: The water steadies under your hands. Sourness, salt and warmth, all as
        they should be once more.
      isPlayer: 0
      portrait: {fileID: 0}
    - speakerName: Haik
      text: Now the reef can heal. Take these seeds. Clear the dead ground at each
        place you tested, then plant them where the rock is clean.
      isPlayer: 0
      portrait: {fileID: 0}
  - key: relic_gift
    lines:
    - speakerName: Haik
      text: The young coral holds. One day fish will shelter here again, and sailors
        will follow them home.
      isPlayer: 0
      portrait: {fileID: 0}
    - speakerName: Haik
      text: You read my waters truly, traveller, and then you healed what you read.
      isPlayer: 0
      portrait: {fileID: 0}
    - speakerName: Haik
      text: Take my compass. Every sailor who called my name steered by it, and it
        never once lied about the way home.
      isPlayer: 0
      portrait: {fileID: 0}
    - speakerName: '{player}'
      text: I'll keep it safe.
      isPlayer: 1
      portrait: {fileID: 0}
    - speakerName: Haik
      text: Keep it steady, too. A day will come when you must find your way through
        waters no one has charted.
      isPlayer: 0
      portrait: {fileID: 0}
  _talkPoint: {fileID: 1187965490}
  _dugongPoint: {fileID: 1704010547}
  _talkCamera: {fileID: 1383252162}
  _frameWithin: 30
  _fadeSeconds: 0.35
  onIntroComplete:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
